# Summer Pasta With Ricotta And Zucchini

Based on [https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/…](https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1017463-summer-pasta-with-zucchini-ricotta-and-basil) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251112185700/https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1017463-summer-pasta-with-zucchini-ricotta-and-basil))

{ rating="3" image="summer_pasta_with_ricotta_and_zucchini.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] [Extra-virgin olive oil]{ ing="extra-virgin-olive-oil" }
- [ ] 1 small [onion]{ ing="onion" }, finely diced
- [ ] 2 lbs [zucchini]{ ing="zucchini" }, sliced into 1/4-inch-thick pieces (for larger zucchini, cut in half lengthwise before slicing)
- [ ] [Salt and pepper]{ ing="salt-and-pepper" }
- [ ] 2 [garlic cloves]{ ing="garlic-cloves" }, minced
- [ ] 1 oz [basil]{ ing="basil" } (about 2 cups loose leaves)
- [ ] 1 lb ziti or [other dry pasta]{ ing="other-dry-pasta" }
- [ ] 8 oz [ricotta]{ ing="ricotta" }
- [ ] Pinch of [crushed red pepper]{ ing="crushed-red-pepper" }
- [ ] [zest of 1 lemon]{ ing="zest-of-1-lemon" }
- [ ] 2 oz [grated Parmesan]{ ing="grated-parmesan" }, pecorino, or a mixture (about 1 cup), plus more for serving

## Recipe

1. Put a pot of water on to boil. In a large skillet over medium-high heat, cook the [onions]{ ing="onion" } in 3 Tbsp [olive oil]{ ing="extra-virgin-olive-oil" } until softened (5-8 min). Reduce heat to keep onions from browning
1. Add [zucchini]{ ing="zucchini" }, season generously with [salt and pepper]{ ing="salt-and-pepper" }, and continue cooking, stirring occasionally until rather soft (about 10 min). Turn off heat
1. Meanwhile, use a mortar and pestle to pound garlic, [basil]{ ing="basil" } and a little salt into a rough paste (or use a mini food processor). Stir in 3 tablespoons [olive oil]{ ing="extra-virgin-olive-oil" }
1. Boil [pasta]{ ing="other-dry-pasta" } per package instructions with the minimum cook time for al dente. Drain, reserving 1 cup of pasta-water
1. In skillet, add [pasta]{ ing="other-dry-pasta" } to [zucchini]{ ing="zucchini" } and turn heat to medium-high
1. Add 1/2 cup [pasta]{ ing="other-dry-pasta" }-water, then [ricotta]{ ing="ricotta" }, [crushed red pepper]{ ing="crushed-red-pepper" }, and [lemon]{ ing="zest-of-1-lemon" } zest, stirring to distribute. Cook for 1 min. Mixture should look creamy. Add a little more pasta water if necessary
1. Add the [basil]{ ing="basil" } paste and half the grated cheese. Quickly stir to incorporate
1. Sprinkle with additional cheese and serve immediately
